{%- comment -%}
  The guarantee, stated once, plainly.

  WHAT THIS REPLACES. This section used to be a two-panel table headed
  "What in-house actually buys you", arguing Lada cloth against sourced
  cloth line by line: yarn count, finish, shrinkage, warranty handling.
  It went because it was the wrong argument in the wrong place. A page
  selling waistcoats does not win by debating a bolt of cloth with the
  shelf next door, and a customer reading a two-column comparison is
  being asked to referee a dispute they did not enter. Worse, half of
  the right-hand column was quietly negative copy about stock the shop
  still sells. The single differentiated thing on that panel, the
  unconditional guarantee, was one bullet among ten.

  So it is now the whole section: one sentence, then three lines that
  answer the only three questions a guarantee raises, which are what
  does it cover, how long does it run, and what do I actually do. No
  badges, no seals, no icons. The three seals live in lada-proof under
  the hero and repeating them here would spend the claim twice.

  THE TWO ACCORDIONS ARE NATIVE AND CARRY NO JAVASCRIPT.
  <details name="lada-info"> is the HTML exclusive-accordion group: the
  browser closes the sibling when you open one, with no script, no
  ARIA to keep in sync and nothing to break if kj-v2.js fails to load.
  The name attribute is unsupported in Safari before 17.2 and Firefox
  before 130, and the fallback there is simply that both panels can be
  open at once. That is harmless by construction: both are in normal
  flow inside a 48ch column, nothing is absolutely positioned, nothing
  overlaps, and the only consequence of two open panels is a slightly
  taller section. Do not add a script to "fix" it.

  WHY MATERIAL AND FABRIC COMPOSITION ARE TWO SEPARATE SETTINGS.
  Because disclosing them separately is the entire point. The trade
  name a cloth is sold under and the fibre content it actually has are
  different facts, and a shop that prints both without being asked has
  said something a shop that prints one blended line has not. Holding
  them in one textarea would let the two collapse back into a single
  marketing string the first time someone edits it, so they cannot
  share a field.

  BOTH VALUES SHIP EMPTY ON PURPOSE, and the cloth panel hides itself
  until at least one cloth fact exists. We do not know Lada's fibre
  content yet, and a section whose thesis is honest disclosure is the
  last place to print an invented percentage. This is the same call
  already made for the opening hours and the landline in lada-house:
  blank until the client says, never guessed. The moment he types them
  the panel appears with no other change.

  TWO SETTINGS DELIBERATELY DO NOT CARRY A `| default:` IN THE MARKUP,
  and the difference is not cosmetic. Everywhere else on this page the
  schema default and a matching `| default:` filter are both present,
  which is fine for copy that must never be empty: clearing the field
  simply puts the sentence back. But `whatsapp` and `care_intro` are
  the two fields whose emptiness is meant to DO something, and a
  `| default:` filter makes that impossible, because Liquid cannot tell
  a field the client cleared from a field he never touched. The first
  version of this section carried `| default: '923019090590'` on the
  number while the schema told him "clear it to drop the link": the
  guard below was dead code and clearing the field silently restored a
  hard-coded number he had just deleted. So the schema default supplies
  the opening value and nothing re-supplies it after that. Clearing the
  number drops the link; clearing the opening line and deleting the
  care blocks drops the whole Care panel.

  THE SHIPPING STATE HAS NO BLOCKS AT ALL. page.lada.json places this
  section with two settings and no blocks, so the preset's four care
  lines are not what the live page gets: they only appear when someone
  adds a fresh copy of the section in the editor. That is why the
  opening line must not count its own list. It used to end "Four things
  keep it that way" above nothing, which is the one thing a section
  about keeping promises cannot do. The default now makes a claim about
  the cloth and stops.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # Clients type telephone numbers the way they say them. The schema
  # asks for a bare number and this quietly accepts the other four
  # spellings rather than emitting a wa.me URL with a plus and three
  # spaces in it, which fails silently on the handset.
  assign wa = section.settings.whatsapp | remove: '+' | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' | remove: '(' | remove: ')'
  assign wa_text = section.settings.whatsapp_text | default: 'I have a question about the Lada guarantee.'
  assign care_intro = section.settings.care_intro

  # The cloth panel is conditional on having something true to say. Two
  # fixed fields plus any number of spec blocks, and if every one of
  # them is empty the whole details element is skipped rather than
  # opened on a blank body. Care is gated the same way, on its opening
  # line or at least one instruction, so neither panel can open onto an
  # empty body and .lada__info is not emitted at all when both are off.
  assign cloth_facts = 0
  if section.settings.material_value != blank
    assign cloth_facts = cloth_facts | plus: 1
  endif
  if section.settings.composition_value != blank
    assign cloth_facts = cloth_facts | plus: 1
  endif
  assign care_lines = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == 'spec' and block.settings.value != blank
      assign cloth_facts = cloth_facts | plus: 1
    endif
    if block.type == 'care' and block.settings.line != blank
      assign care_lines = care_lines | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
  assign show_care = false
  if care_intro != blank or care_lines > 0
    assign show_care = true
  endif
-%}
<section class="lada" id="lada-promise" aria-labelledby="lada-promise-h">
  <div class="lada__wrap lada__sec">

    <div class="lada__promise-block">
      <p class="lada__kicker">{{ section.settings.kicker | default: 'Plainly put' }}</p>
      <h2 class="lada__h2" id="lada-promise-h">{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'The guarantee, in plain words' }}</h2>
      <p class="lada__promise-lede">
        {{ section.settings.guarantee | default: 'If a Lada piece ever fails, in the cloth or in the making, we replace it or refund it, with no conditions and no time limit.' }}
      </p>

      <dl class="lada__terms">
        <div>
          <dt>{{ section.settings.term1_label | default: 'What it covers' }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ section.settings.term1_value | default: 'The cloth and the making, on every Lada piece, whether we cut it to your measurement or you took it off the rail.' }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>{{ section.settings.term2_label | default: 'How long it runs' }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ section.settings.term2_value | default: 'For as long as you own the piece. There is no window to miss and no receipt to find.' }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>{{ section.settings.term3_label | default: 'How to claim' }}</dt>
          <dd>
            {{ section.settings.term3_value | default: 'Bring it in to the shop, or send us a photograph on WhatsApp and we will tell you what happens next.' }}
            {%- comment -%}
              The link needs its own block box and cannot simply follow
              the sentence. .lada__link is display:inline-block in
              kj-v2.css, so left inline it joins the last line of the
              sentence, and the margin that keeps its completing
              underline off the row's closing hairline then shifts it
              down INSIDE that line box, staggering it against the text
              beside it. The span makes it a line of its own; the
              anchor stays inline-block so the underline still measures
              the words rather than the whole 48ch column.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if wa != blank -%}
              <span class="lada__terms-cta">
                <a class="lada__link" href="https://wa.me/{{ wa }}?text={{ wa_text | url_encode }}"
                   target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                  {{- section.settings.wa_label | default: 'Message us on WhatsApp' -}}</a>
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Titles at 12px/600, sentence case, drawn as hairlines with a
      plus that loses its upright stroke on open. No card, no shadow,
      no fill: khaadi's rule that the information architecture is
      drawn entirely with lines, which is also what keeps two panels
      from reading as two more marketing tiles under a guarantee.
      Closed by default, both of them.

      THE TITLE INSIDE THE SUMMARY IS A REAL h3. <summary>'s content
      model is phrasing content optionally intermixed with heading
      content, so this is valid HTML, and it is the only way a screen
      reader user gets to jump between the two panels instead of
      arrowing through the guarantee to find them. It is the same
      shape the ARIA authoring practices give a scripted accordion,
      a button inside a heading, done with the native element. The
      page's one h1 is in lada-hero and the section h2 is above, so
      h3 is the correct next rung, not a size choice: .lada__acc-t
      takes its type from the summary and has none of its own.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if cloth_facts > 0 or show_care -%}
    <div class="lada__info">

      {%- if cloth_facts > 0 -%}
        <details class="lada__acc" name="lada-info">
          <summary class="lada__acc-h">
            <h3 class="lada__acc-t">{{ section.settings.cloth_title | default: 'Cloth and construction' }}</h3>
            <span class="lada__acc-ind" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="lada__acc-body">
            <dl class="lada__spec">
              {%- if section.settings.material_value != blank -%}
                <div>
                  <dt>{{ section.settings.material_label | default: 'Material' }}</dt>
                  <dd>{{ section.settings.material_value }}</dd>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if section.settings.composition_value != blank -%}
                <div>
                  <dt>{{ section.settings.composition_label | default: 'Fabric composition' }}</dt>
                  <dd>{{ section.settings.composition_value }}</dd>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  The label falls back to a word rather than to nothing.
                  A dl row cannot drop its dt without going malformed,
                  and dt carries min-width:11ch, so a cleared label
                  would leave a measured blank column beside the fact.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if block.type == 'spec' and block.settings.value != blank -%}
                  <div {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <dt>{{ block.settings.label | default: 'Detail' }}</dt>
                    <dd>{{ block.settings.value }}</dd>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </dl>
          </div>
        </details>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if show_care -%}
      <details class="lada__acc" name="lada-info">
        <summary class="lada__acc-h">
          <h3 class="lada__acc-t">{{ section.settings.care_title | default: 'Care' }}</h3>
          <span class="lada__acc-ind" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="lada__acc-body">
          {%- if care_intro != blank -%}
            <p class="lada__care-intro">{{ care_intro }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if care_lines > 0 -%}
            <ul class="lada__care">
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- if block.type == 'care' and block.settings.line != blank -%}
                  <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ block.settings.line }}</li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </details>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Lada promise",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "One centred block: the guarantee in one sentence, then three lines. No badges, no icons, no comparison table." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "kicker", "label": "Kicker", "default": "Plainly put" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "The guarantee, in plain words" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "guarantee", "label": "The guarantee", "info": "One sentence. It is the line the whole section exists to carry, so keep it to one.", "default": "If a Lada piece ever fails, in the cloth or in the making, we replace it or refund it, with no conditions and no time limit." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The three lines" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Labels are drawn in small capitals by the page. Type them in sentence case." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "term1_label", "label": "Line 1 label", "default": "What it covers" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "term1_value", "label": "Line 1 text", "default": "The cloth and the making, on every Lada piece, whether we cut it to your measurement or you took it off the rail." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "term2_label", "label": "Line 2 label", "default": "How long it runs" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "term2_value", "label": "Line 2 text", "default": "For as long as you own the piece. There is no window to miss and no receipt to find." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "term3_label", "label": "Line 3 label", "default": "How to claim" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "term3_value", "label": "Line 3 text", "default": "Bring it in to the shop, or send us a photograph on WhatsApp and we will tell you what happens next." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "wa_label", "label": "WhatsApp link", "default": "Message us on WhatsApp" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "whatsapp", "label": "WhatsApp number", "info": "Country code first. A plus, spaces or dashes are stripped for you. Clear the field to drop the link.", "default": "923019090590" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "whatsapp_text", "label": "Pre-filled message", "default": "I have a question about the Lada guarantee." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Cloth and construction" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The trade name and the real fibre content are two separate fields on purpose: printing both, unasked, is the whole point. Both are empty until you fill them, and the panel stays hidden while they are, because a guessed percentage on a page about honesty is worse than no panel." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cloth_title", "label": "Panel title", "default": "Cloth and construction" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "material_label", "label": "Trade name label", "default": "Material" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "material_value", "label": "Trade name", "info": "What the cloth is sold as, for example Raw silk." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "composition_label", "label": "Composition label", "default": "Fabric composition" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "composition_value", "label": "Composition", "info": "The honest fibre content, for example 70% viscose, 30% polyester. Needed before launch." },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Add a Cloth fact block for anything else: weave, lining, made in." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Care" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "care_title", "label": "Panel title", "default": "Care" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "care_intro", "label": "Opening line", "info": "Do not count the instructions in this line. The page ships with none of them and the count would be wrong.", "default": "The cloth is washed, pressed and shrunk before it is cut, so it will not move on you." },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Add a Care line block for each instruction. Drag to reorder. Clear the opening line and delete every care block and the whole Care panel disappears." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "spec", "name": "Cloth fact", "settings": [
      { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "info": "Drawn in small capitals. Type it in sentence case.", "default": "Made in" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "value", "label": "Value", "info": "The row is hidden while this is empty.", "default": "Sheikhupura, Pakistan" }
    ]},
    { "type": "care", "name": "Care line", "settings": [
      { "type": "text", "id": "line", "label": "Instruction", "default": "Dry clean only." }
    ]}
  ],
  "max_blocks": 12,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Lada promise",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "spec", "settings": { "label": "Made in", "value": "Sheikhupura, Pakistan" } },
        { "type": "care", "settings": { "line": "Dry clean only." } },
        { "type": "care", "settings": { "line": "Press on a low iron, on the reverse, with a cloth between." } },
        { "type": "care", "settings": { "line": "Hang it on a broad wooden hanger, never on wire." } },
        { "type": "care", "settings": { "line": "Store it dry and aired, out of plastic." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
